{
    "word": "concupiscence",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
                "word": "concupiscence",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1592874d-811c-4299-8654-5b2756b62256",
                        "entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "concupiscences"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                        "entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ardent desire, especially sexual desire; lust."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14213700-67a6-4fc8-ad45-1a1cdb3c2bf2",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "[Y]it haue vvee one thing in our ſelues and of our ſelues, (euen originall ſinne, concupiſcence or luſt) vvhich neuer ceaſeth too egge vs and allure vs from God, and too ſtaine vs vvith all kinde of vnclennes: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "881a05af-d0c4-43e1-9b09-6268f77dc971",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "for as St. Jerome observes, it is to shew that the true Christian not setting his heart upon the goods of the Earth, ought to trample under foot, all Avarice and immoderate concupiscence of corruptible riches: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fe80d66-4ce7-47d5-8d09-ee72c8ecdb20",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "Poor Miss Tita's sense of her failure had produced an extraordinary alteration in her, but I had been too full of my literary concupiscence to think of that. Now I perceived it; I can scarcely tell how it startled me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5c71e30-293a-4101-ab6d-be5f9c4473fa",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "He was torn by two intense and conflicting desires: his ardent wish to advance through his association with Mr. Browning, and his concupiscence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ce72452-c211-48e7-bce2-74e6e37230c9",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "Skaters, spinning like atoms across fields of pure light, are desirable in a way that transcends mere concupiscence; they inhabit another element, and the man who would try to catch one risks, literally, falling on his ass."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "718a67bb-4aa9-4448-878b-9214b9ee7489",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "Quite certainly you command me to refrain from concupiscence of the flesh and concupiscence of the eyes and worldy pride."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58f19da3-5fd2-4569-b480-ef2f3be389f0",
                                "sense_id": "3904d438-b9db-3e73-838e-a9d8503f771d",
                                "text": "America insulted the rest of the planet, thought Malik Solanka in his old-fashioned way, by treating such bounty with the shoulder-shrugging casualness of the inequitably wealthy. But New York in this time of plenty had become the object and goal of the world’s concupiscence and lust, and the “insult” only made the rest of the planet more desirous than ever."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "106551d5-f5f9-30c9-a677-9e26066fd15d",
                        "entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "the desire of a person's lower appetite, contrary to reason, which subjugates and inclines them to experience temptation and to give in to sin, due to the Fall and original sin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87981daf-65f8-48f9-8072-d2da49f3ed4d",
                                "sense_id": "106551d5-f5f9-30c9-a677-9e26066fd15d",
                                "text": "[“]Since concupiscence is the most common form of temptation, it is better for him to know something about it. The soul cannot be humbled by fasts and prayer; it must be broken by mortal sin to experience forgiveness of sin and rise to a state of grace. Otherwise, religion is nothing but dead logic.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95d6d3a4-37ea-40bb-9212-2706faea9aee",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
                        "source_sense_description": "Ardent desire",
                        "target_lang_word": "begeerte",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "begeerte",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "489f3ae6-2ae1-302d-b942-dc229b4148cd",
                                        "entry_id": "0f62b729-f1af-3c09-9830-fcfe9fb5ac5e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "sterk verlangen naar iets, hebzucht"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db4d37b6-bcf2-43e5-a433-5bdaa917cdfc",
                                                "sense_id": "489f3ae6-2ae1-302d-b942-dc229b4148cd",
                                                "text": "De reclame voor de nieuwe auto wekte een grote begeerte bij hem op."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "529a522b-5f98-4321-8e20-b73324722caf",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
                        "source_sense_description": "Ardent desire",
                        "target_lang_word": "concupiscence",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "concupiscence",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                        "entry_id": "5d42c1fa-46b0-34e2-b71b-c62a9d57093a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Envie, inclination violente aux plaisirs qui sont interdits par les moralistes, surtout aux plaisirs sexuels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "948532d1-bae7-46fc-92f7-44ed50c01523",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "Elle est en ce moment dans le bois d’oliviers, et les gardes (vos gardes, Taxis) font calmer par elle leurs concupiscences pendant les intervalles de recherches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4542832-4b12-4e42-8bc5-e3a91dbd131f",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "Le mot de concupiscence charnelle, pareil à un lourd crapaud élastique, n’a de plein sens que si on l’applique aux familles poussées à même le sol. Les lourds repliements d’appétits sensuels, les énormes convoitises tapies des années durant, ne sont possibles qu’à la campagne, où les maisons sont encore des êtres qui s’observent, se haïssent, gémissent au même souffle d’air et se frôlent et se bousculent dans le travail de leurs bras occupés à remuer la terre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "038d6770-450c-49e3-9211-25e0b4f54c07",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "[…] des messieurs, […], auscultaient des paumes les charmes de ces demoiselles servantes, impassibles mais souriantes. Il y avait aussi des femmes qui les expertisaient d'un doigt agile, les yeux endiamantés de concupiscence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0943379-f2f2-41d5-a523-b73bc1bc6332",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "Et chacun de me plaisanter ; ma jeunesse à son lever, mon parfum de fille fraîche, ma chair toute neuve en son premier éclat éveillaient chez les hommes de sournoises concupiscences, aiguisaient leur regard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecfb6c34-0a86-44c0-ba93-ff6dc69a6c60",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "D’ailleurs M. le Doyen n’a peut-être pas tort quand il répète : Simon, ce n’est pas au démon de la concupiscence qu’il a affaire, mais à celui de l’ambition. Il ne regarde guère les filles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efd85000-a8ff-46c4-836a-52eadc934d7e",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "Pomme attirait souvent les regards, remarqua un jour le futur conservateur. Et c’étaient des regards sans équivoque, d’une franche concupiscence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "623a0a32-8744-47e3-bdd4-6a4734078296",
                                                "sense_id": "73536cc2-c485-35a9-bdc8-578f07c2c22f",
                                                "text": "Il préférait la musique classique et les chemisettes à carreaux mais, pour attirer les concupiscences, il devait avoir la tenue wesh-wesh, l'allure racaille, la casquette Nike, visière retournée en prime."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17548bcd-1556-47d7-96d0-c93e60836b4b",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f86c3e5-9b2c-3e16-9e47-8aabbf896f8e",
